# Confine PostgreSQL behavior to adapters and repositories

# Engine and profile boundary

The generated repository has one fixed persistence profile: PostgreSQL with async SQLAlchemy and
Alembic.
Keep PostgreSQL and migration-tool knowledge inside `schema/`, the profile adapter/database module,
and repository implementations. API, application/service, and domain policy code use profile-neutral
interfaces and types.

Centralize mappings for public identifiers, timezone-aware timestamps, native JSON, transaction
isolation, constraint-error translation, and connection/session creation. Do not scatter raw engine
types, driver imports, dialect SQL, or migration-tool commands through business services.

Raw SQL is permitted only in the repository/adapter boundary or reviewed migrations, must be
parameterized, and must use named constants for non-obvious sentinel/enum values. Runtime code must
not execute DDL. Services do not issue cross-database queries or database links.

Another ORM, migration system, persistence engine, or runtime-selectable adapter is forbidden. A
cache adapter is added later only as part of a complete accepted capability; it is not an empty
profile promise. The fixed profile scaffolds, migrates, tests, exports contracts, and validates
drift through one quality gate.
